  "production": [
    "New loginAction operation uses the existing OriginalTraditionalRuntime/RuntimeTask/RuleEnvironment/Rhino and finite OriginalSourceLoginHost. Existing source library/loginJS prefixes the authored action, no implicit login() suffix, actual real Java result Map, null standalone book/chapter, exact isLongClick Boolean. Action completion is ignored; no header inferred.",
    "Null action or getLoginJs=null skips evaluation. Empty nonnull action still evaluates the prelude. Empty working Map remains an actual empty action map and never triggers the form-login removal path. Browser login/action/v2 remain explicit unsupported in native action API; existing App external http(s) path is retained.",
    "Same Package executeOriginal transport/Native preview executor/service source actor/revision/deadline/cancel/effects; no owner, parser, cache, engine, VM or global fallback added. Existing sensitive RuntimeTask operation set covers loginAction before evaluation and safe code/effect metadata crosses the new UI boundary.",
    "Traditional Grid original action sends the complete values snapshot with only visible text/password default overlay through originalFormSubmissionValues. Hidden keys and explicit empty edits survive. Traditional select changes/actions no longer call storeLoginInfo. Nontraditional/TTS branches retain their existing callbacks/behavior.",
    "A form with button rows uses doLogin/originalFormLogin on original OK, preserving full map and the existing accepted-save/login/success-dismiss behavior. Nontraditional toolbar save/close stays on its prior path. Full hasChange/oKToClose dismissal migration is not claimed.",
    "Original button/toggle pointer gesture emits one short or long action after release; toggle cycles before action. Shared Grid uptime timestamp filters pointer releases within200ms across buttons/toggles before cycle/dispatch. Accessibility/keyboard Button action bypasses pointer gate; select callback is outside that gate. This is source wiring, not actual SwiftUI interaction acceptance.",
    "Owned originalActionTask/generation cancel on load/disappear and guard terminal publication. The reused formSubmissionTask now has its own generation: load/disappear rotate before cancelling, classification/success/catch/defer cannot clear newer handles/loading or publish old alerts. Existing source executor still drains and preserves accepted owner effects.",
    "The existing finite host remains byte-unchanged: upLoginData/reLoginView/refreshExplore/toast/browser UI methods throw typed unsupported. No callback is silently ignored, converted to fake success, written to Keychain, stored in a deduplicated effects set or synchronously reentered into the locked source actor."
  ],
